config: turn off services that only work for the official app

- CHECK_UPDATES=false: update checks return the official app's updates.
- SUPPORTS_PASSKEYS=false: upstream notes that passkeys work only on
  official app ids.
- SAFETYNET_KEY="": the upstream key belongs to the official app. An empty
  key already switches LoginActivity to the path without SafetyNet.
- PLAYSTORE_APP_URL now points to this fork's releases page, so "update"
  links do not send users to the official app.
>>> replace_line TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/messenger/BuildVars.java
>>> find
public static boolean CHECK_UPDATES =
>>> text
    public static boolean CHECK_UPDATES = false; // unofficial client: update checks refer to the official app
>>> replace_line TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/messenger/BuildVars.java
>>> find
public static String SAFETYNET_KEY =
>>> text
    public static String SAFETYNET_KEY = ""; // unofficial client: the upstream key is bound to the official app
>>> replace_line TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/messenger/BuildVars.java
>>> find
public static String PLAYSTORE_APP_URL =
>>> text
    public static String PLAYSTORE_APP_URL = "https://github.com/3x-nin/Telegram/releases"; // unofficial client: no Play Store listing
